[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mistersilver-uk/fabricate/pulls/1421","id":4406853885,"node_id":"PR_kwDORPgBts8AAAABBqtA_Q","html_url":"https://github.com/mistersilver-uk/fabricate/pull/1421","diff_url":"https://github.com/mistersilver-uk/fabricate/pull/1421.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mistersilver-uk/fabricate/pull/1421.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mistersilver-uk/fabricate/issues/1421","number":1421,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"docs: align the reviewer skill's reference list with main","user":{"login":"mistersilver-uk","id":17074386,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MDc0Mzg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17074386?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistersilver-uk","html_url":"https://github.com/mistersilver-uk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistersilver-uk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistersilver-uk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistersilver-uk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistersilver-uk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistersilver-uk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistersilver-uk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistersilver-uk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistersilver-uk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mistersilver-uk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Prerequisite for #1418, task 1. **Merge this with a merge commit, and merge it before the `release` ruleset is created.**\n\n## Why this PR exists\n\n#1418 replaces the forward-port's content gate — today an unverified human assertion that files \"were authored through a reviewed pull request\" — with a mechanical check that every commit is attributable to a merged pull request **based on `release`**.\n\nPlan review found that check cannot be tested, because **there is no merged pull request based on `release` anywhere in this repository's history**. Every release-line change to date arrived either as a CI `--no-ff` promote merge or, for the v1.9.1 and v1.9.2 hotfixes, as a direct push. So the verifier's positive control would have to be fabricated — a real payload with `baseRefName` hand-edited to `\"release\"` — which is exactly the looser-than-reality fixture that hid a live defect in this repository for a whole feature's lifetime.\n\nThis PR creates the real thing. Once merged, the association payload it produces is captured verbatim as the committed fixture behind #1418's positive-control test. The payload's shape does not depend on whether the commit touched files, so an empty commit yields the same fixture a file-touching one would.\n\n## Why the commit is empty\n\nThe first attempt carried real content: `.agents/skills/fabricate-reviewer/SKILL.md` taken verbatim from `main`, chosen as the smallest divergence between the two lines. CI refused it, and the refusal was correct:\n\n```\nAgent binding validation failed (3):\n  - .agents/skills/fabricate-reviewer/SKILL.md: references missing path `openspec/specs/design-system/spec.md`\n  - .agents/skills/fabricate-reviewer/SKILL.md: references missing path `openspec/specs/design-system/library.html`\n  - .agents/skills/fabricate-reviewer/SKILL.md: references missing path `scripts/lib/designSystemPrimitives.json`\n```\n\nThat bullet is valid on `main` and **dangling on `release`** — all three paths arrived with design-system work that landed after v1.9.2 was cut. The lesson generalises, and is worth recording for #1418: *byte-identical to `main`* is not sufficient for content landing on `release`, because content can be internally valid there and still depend on other `main`-only content.\n\nEvery other candidate had the same problem or a worse one. The remaining text divergences are all **deletions** — bringing `release` to `main`'s version would remove documentation pages from the release line — and the rest are binary assets.\n\nEmpty is therefore not a shortcut but the only content that satisfies every constraint at once:\n\n- **It cannot dangle**, because it references nothing.\n- **It leaves `release`'s tree untouched**, so the next forward-port still computes an empty `git diff --stat origin/main` and takes its existing fast path. A capture PR carrying novel content would trip the very gate #1418 exists to fix and demand another manual merge.\n- **It still produces a genuine merged-PR-based-on-`release` association**, which is the entire point.\n\n## What merging it does not do\n\nNothing is minted. `release.yml` gates `publish-s3`, `verify-publish` and `forward-port` on `needs.semantic-release.outputs.next_version != ''`, and a `docs:` commit triggers no release under `release.config.js`, so semantic-release computes no version and every downstream job is skipped.\n\n## Follow-up already tracked\n\n#1418 records that this fixture is replaced with one captured from a genuine hotfix at the next release-line fix, so the positive control eventually rests on a commit that carried real content.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_016qJYZEoNFWq1iNCy5Us4Ln\n","created_at":"2026-08-31T22:27:09Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T07:48:22Z","closed_at":"2026-09-01T07:48:19Z","merged_at":"2026-09-01T07:48:19Z","merge_commit_sha":"74e0988f16f63a7c6e9be4add94eb94c5d762b10","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mistersilver-uk/fabricate/pulls/1421/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mistersilver-uk/fabricate/pulls/1421/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mistersilver-uk/fabricate/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mistersilver-uk/fabricate/issues/1421/com